      "side": 1,
      "message": "This test is based on role assignments on projects and _create_projects_hierarchy does not returns a clean project hierarchy, since it puts self.project_id as the root of the hierarchy, and there is already a role assignment on this project, defined on the sample data.\n\nIt could be confusing to someone reading it to understand why I am just adding on a role assignment in the subproject and project if I want it on all \u0027created\u0027 projects.\nIf we wanted to clarify this, I should make the comment a line 712 bigger to say there are something that already exists.\n\nI know using that method would save lines, but waste time from reviewers and maintainers, which is expensive.\n\nAs I stated on a comment in the previous patch set, anyone can fell free to submit a bug and fix that method, that could return a \u0027clean\u0027 hierarchy. I am not doing this as part of this patch since it is not related to the proposed change.",
